WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.458 --> 00:00:02.002
Hey there, space explorers!

00:00:02.252 --> 00:00:04.129
Today, you and the Peanuts gang will

00:00:04.129 --> 00:00:06.339
take on three exciting S.T.E.M. missions

00:00:06.548 --> 00:00:08.341
inspired by Snoopy in Space.

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:10.385
Collecting space samples,

00:00:10.885 --> 00:00:12.262
building a stellar satellite,

00:00:12.637 --> 00:00:14.264
and crafting moon sand.

00:00:14.556 --> 00:00:15.724
I can’t go to space!

00:00:15.932 --> 00:00:17.308
I don’t have my toothbrush!

00:00:17.642 --> 00:00:19.436
Feel free to attempt all of them,

00:00:19.477 --> 00:00:20.395
or just your favorite.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.063
It’s up to you and your team!

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:23.648
So, gather the parts you’ll need,

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:25.191
grab a grown-up to help,

00:00:25.316 --> 00:00:26.985
and get ready to blast off.

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:28.361
Are we ready to launch?

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:29.195
Ready!

00:00:29.404 --> 00:00:29.904
Ready!

00:00:30.071 --> 00:00:30.571
Ready!

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:32.866
[Snoring]

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:34.951
Sir? Sir!

00:00:37.954 --> 00:00:38.705
Present!

00:00:40.623 --> 00:00:43.543
Mission One: Galaxy Slime

00:00:46.629 --> 00:00:48.465
The galaxy is pretty big.

00:00:50.842 --> 00:00:52.343
All: Woah!

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:54.679
First, gather your materials.

00:00:56.473 --> 00:00:58.016
A ½ cup of clear glue,

00:00:58.475 --> 00:00:59.559
a ½ cup of water,

00:01:00.018 --> 00:01:01.895
a ½ cup of liquid cornstarch,

00:01:02.103 --> 00:01:02.771
food coloring,

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:04.773
glitter and confetti stars,

00:01:04.981 --> 00:01:06.399
and a large bowl and spoon

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:07.650
to mix it all together.

00:01:09.486 --> 00:01:11.863
First, mix the water and glue in your bowl.

00:01:16.951 --> 00:01:19.037
Next, add a drop or two

00:01:19.037 --> 00:01:20.747
of your favorite food coloring,

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:23.416
and plenty of glitter and stars.

00:01:27.128 --> 00:01:29.881
Now, add the liquid cornstarch

00:01:30.799 --> 00:01:33.093
and stir until there’s no liquid left.

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:38.681
Your bowl should now be

00:01:38.681 --> 00:01:41.351
totally full of galaxy slime!

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:43.853
Woo-hoo! Yeah! 

00:01:43.978 --> 00:01:46.606
Start experimenting with your galaxy slime

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:48.274
by kneading and playing with it.

00:01:50.819 --> 00:01:52.821
You should notice the slime feeling different

00:01:52.821 --> 00:01:53.863
the more you play with it.

00:01:55.198 --> 00:01:56.658
How far can you stretch it?

00:01:57.075 --> 00:01:58.076
I can’t wait to see what

00:01:58.076 --> 00:01:59.244
discoveries they’ve made!

00:01:59.452 --> 00:02:00.411
Like all the aliens

00:02:00.411 --> 00:02:01.746
they’re hiding in the basement?

00:02:02.497 --> 00:02:03.456
Good grief.

00:02:05.041 --> 00:02:07.794
Our next mission is Preflight Satellite.

00:02:11.714 --> 00:02:13.299
Now I’m hoping to get a transmission

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:15.593
from even farther in space!

00:02:16.219 --> 00:02:17.178
Here’s what you’ll need:

00:02:17.387 --> 00:02:18.388
a juice box,

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:19.389
some sponges,

00:02:19.681 --> 00:02:20.807
a few pipe cleaners,

00:02:21.099 --> 00:02:21.891
a pick-up stick,

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:23.226
a paper straw,

00:02:23.685 --> 00:02:24.769
a Styrofoam ball,

00:02:25.061 --> 00:02:26.146
black construction paper,

00:02:26.563 --> 00:02:27.480
washers &amp; bolts,

00:02:27.814 --> 00:02:28.314
tape,

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:30.024
and, finally, scissors.

00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:31.985
So, what do we do now?

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:33.278
Let’s start building!

00:02:34.154 --> 00:02:35.780
First, wrap the juice box

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:37.407
in your favorite colorful paper.

00:02:39.826 --> 00:02:41.619
A juice box makes a great container

00:02:41.744 --> 00:02:43.496
for all your scientific instruments.

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:47.500
In this section, we’re going to be

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:48.960
working with safety scissors.

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:50.962
So, grab an adult and have them

00:02:50.962 --> 00:02:53.047
cut the sponges into three pieces.

00:02:54.716 --> 00:02:57.010
The sponges will make perfect solar panels

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:58.344
to soak up sunlight.

00:02:59.137 --> 00:03:00.972
Now, run the pipe cleaners

00:03:00.972 --> 00:03:02.265
through each sponge,

00:03:04.934 --> 00:03:06.477
and then into the juice box.

00:03:08.813 --> 00:03:10.023
If you need help making holes

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:10.815
in the juice box,

00:03:11.107 --> 00:03:11.858
ask an adult!

00:03:14.152 --> 00:03:15.195
Tilt the sponges,

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:16.779
or your satellite’s panels,

00:03:17.197 --> 00:03:19.324
to capture maximum sunlight power.

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:21.242
All: Ooh! Woah!

00:03:21.451 --> 00:03:22.493
Now, it’s time to

00:03:22.493 --> 00:03:24.037
assemble your communications

00:03:24.245 --> 00:03:25.455
by having an adult cut

00:03:25.455 --> 00:03:27.040
the Styrofoam ball in half.

00:03:27.415 --> 00:03:29.459
And they can also cut a small circle of

00:03:29.459 --> 00:03:31.127
black construction paper for you.

00:03:34.255 --> 00:03:36.466
And glue it to the flat surface of the foam.

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:45.892
Then, take a small part of the straw

00:03:45.892 --> 00:03:47.727
and stick it through the black paper

00:03:47.727 --> 00:03:48.561
into the foam.

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:51.648
Creating a communication dish!

00:03:52.941 --> 00:03:53.942
Grab a pick-up stick

00:03:53.942 --> 00:03:55.652
and push one end into the foam,

00:03:58.112 --> 00:04:00.323
and the other into the top of the juice box.

00:04:03.993 --> 00:04:04.994
Now your satellite can

00:04:04.994 --> 00:04:06.996
stay in contact with ground control!

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:08.581
Snoopy, do you copy?

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:11.668
To make sure your satellite

00:04:11.668 --> 00:04:12.585
doesn’t get lost,

00:04:12.877 --> 00:04:14.837
it’ll need an orientation tracker

00:04:14.837 --> 00:04:16.297
to keep an eye on the stars.

00:04:18.258 --> 00:04:19.217
Your washers will be

00:04:19.217 --> 00:04:20.260
the perfect trackers

00:04:20.468 --> 00:04:22.011
once you tape them to the box.

00:04:26.808 --> 00:04:28.142
Time to launch and

00:04:28.142 --> 00:04:29.435
drift through space!

00:04:30.103 --> 00:04:34.023
[Everyone cheers]

00:04:35.566 --> 00:04:37.527
Our final mission is critical.

00:04:38.111 --> 00:04:39.070
Crater Creator.

00:04:43.283 --> 00:04:44.534
Ooh!

00:04:44.534 --> 00:04:45.368
Here’s what you’ll need

00:04:45.368 --> 00:04:47.328
to create some moon sand craters:

00:04:47.537 --> 00:04:49.455
2 ½ cups of colorful sand,

00:04:49.664 --> 00:04:50.164
glitter,

00:04:50.415 --> 00:04:51.958
1 ½ cups of cornstarch,

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:53.668
¾ cup of canola oil,

00:04:54.043 --> 00:04:55.753
and a large mixing bowl and spoon.

00:04:56.379 --> 00:04:57.714
What are we waiting for?

00:04:58.339 --> 00:04:59.966
Okay, step one -

00:05:00.341 --> 00:05:02.176
pour all of your sand into a bowl.

00:05:07.015 --> 00:05:08.975
We’re combining blue and black sand,

00:05:09.225 --> 00:05:10.601
but use any colors you like

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:11.477
and mix it up!

00:05:13.354 --> 00:05:14.022
Step two,

00:05:14.272 --> 00:05:15.940
slowly add in the cornstarch

00:05:16.107 --> 00:05:18.109
one or two spoonfuls at a time.

00:05:20.278 --> 00:05:21.070
Step three,

00:05:21.404 --> 00:05:23.531
slowly pour in the canola oil.

00:05:27.410 --> 00:05:29.037
And step four is the most fun!

00:05:29.454 --> 00:05:30.121
Add glitter,

00:05:31.414 --> 00:05:32.707
and mix it all together.

00:05:36.544 --> 00:05:38.463
Next, grab an adult and transfer

00:05:38.463 --> 00:05:39.422
your moon sand to

00:05:39.422 --> 00:05:40.965
a new container if you’d like.

00:05:43.509 --> 00:05:45.845
Add craters, mountains, canyons,

00:05:48.014 --> 00:05:49.390
and colorful decorations!

00:05:53.394 --> 00:05:55.104
It never hurts to add more glitter, too!

00:05:55.605 --> 00:05:56.522
Now you and your team

00:05:56.522 --> 00:05:59.025
have your very own moonscape to explore.

00:06:02.111 --> 00:06:02.820
[Snoopy yells]

00:06:09.243 --> 00:06:10.370
Great job today!

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:12.580
[Cheering]

00:06:12.580 --> 00:06:13.748
Great work, everyone!

00:06:13.956 --> 00:06:15.458
Now you have all the tools

00:06:15.458 --> 00:06:17.668
to make any mission a success.

00:06:17.668 --> 00:06:18.878
[Cheering]

00:06:18.878 --> 00:06:20.213
I’m swept up in the moment!

00:06:20.338 --> 00:06:21.297
All that’s left

00:06:21.297 --> 00:06:22.965
is to get out and explore.

00:06:23.091 --> 00:06:24.258
Our solar system is a

00:06:24.258 --> 00:06:26.052
vast and wonderous place.

00:06:29.597 --> 00:06:32.600
Snoopy in Space: The Search for Life.

